-- CHANGE SET F — Sensitive-column access restrictions
-- Lexicographic step 4 / 10. Payroll/biometric row policies follow in 00045.
-- Depends on: C HR salary RPC live so admin forms can still display salary.
-- App in the same release (not this mission):
--   frontend/src/contexts/app-context.tsx users select must become an
--   explicit column list that omits salary, nin, bank_*, face_biometric.
-- Pattern matches schools.paystack_secret_key (20260819000000).
-- C1: no auth.uid() in this file.
-- C3: G must re-REVOKE these columns after any table-level GRANT UPDATE.

REVOKE SELECT, UPDATE (
  salary, nin, bank_name, account_number, account_name, face_biometric
) ON public.users FROM PUBLIC, anon, authenticated;

-- service_role retains table ALL. Do not GRANT the sensitive columns back
-- to authenticated for "own row" — B6: no self salary/bank on the profile
-- endpoint. PostgREST omits revoked columns from select=*.

-- Expected catalog after this file (before G):
--   authenticated: no SELECT/UPDATE on the six columns
--   anon / PUBLIC: no SELECT/UPDATE on the six columns
--   service_role: table ALL still includes them
-- G (00080) re-asserts this after table GRANT UPDATE on users.
